SUMMARY:WNC Sierra Club 10/7: This Fall’s Election - What's at Stake?
DESCRIPTION:WNC Sierra Club\nJoin us Oct. 7 as Ken Brame\, who serves as t
 he WNC Sierra Club Political Co-Chair\, talks about what's at stake in the
  2026 midterm elections. His presentation will cover what's happening nati
 onally\, in North Carolina\, and locally. Learn more about:\n\n* Which rac
 es will be most competitive\;\n* What the political climate looks like\;\n
 * What the potential outcomes are\;\n* The implications for the environmen
 t\;\n* How you can get involved and make a difference.\n\nKen Brame is the
  former chair of both the national Sierra Club Political Committee and the
  NC Sierra Club Political Committee.\n\nThe WNC Sierra Club meets monthly 
 in Room 102 at UNCA’s Reuter Center on Campus Drive and simultaneously o
 n [Zoom](https://unca-edu.zoom.us/j/85189349413?pwd=QmorsXPwjbS0BgiLR7xLIt
 F3M1atab.1).\n\n**Parking at UNC Asheville:** If you do not have a parking
  sticker from OLLI\, you'll need to register for parking either ahead of t
 ime at [unca.aimsparking.com](https://unca.aimsparking.com/) or at the Reu
 ter Center on the night of the meeting. The latest information about fees 
 and requirements can be found at that link. There are no visitor fees afte
 r 5 p.m.
